{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/304560-book-of-the-deceived-errata-thread","id":304560,"title":"Book of the Deceived errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-06T07:50:30-08:00","id":304560,"title":"Book of the Deceived errata thread","content":"Please report any typos or visual glitches in <i>Book of the Deceived</i> here. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:14:25-08:00","id":304610,"title":"","content":"Page 9, Table of Contents - &quot;Introduction: Damnable Lies&quot; <b>Should be bolded to match other headers.</b><br /> <br /> Page 10, Table of Contents - &quot;Chapter <b>ThreeUnder</b> Wandering Stars&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 69, Left Column, Third Paragraph - &quot;The Shan\u2019iatu questioned the woman and she, who had <b>sword</b> loyalty to the Keeper in the language he taught her, screamed like many different beasts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:57:25-08:00","id":304650,"title":"","content":"Page 30: &quot;When all stars dim and the firmament unravels, it is I shall compose the lone and final epitaph.&quot;<br /> <br /> Missing the word &quot;who&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 71: &quot;IMPURE SYLLABLE<br /> Prerequisites: Guild Status (Akhem-Urtu) \u25cf, Ren 3&quot;<br /> <br /> The prerequisites should not have Ren 3. All Deceived have Ren 5 and this is a Guild Affinity, so the pillar requirement is not only redundant but inappropriate for the type of Affinity this is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","user":"Nephilpal","date":".  More edits found. 11-06-2014, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:03:16-08:00","id":304653,"title":"","content":"Page 87, Immortal Names, Second paragraph -&quot;...and those that <b>do function</b> less effectively or require greater effort to succeed&quot; I believe there should be a coma there.<br /> <br /> Page 94, As Whisper in the Nigth - &quot;that <b>theLost</b> Guild exists&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 155, &quot;..six additional Deceived, one for each of the Deceived guilds&quot; - Deceived don't have guilds, it is a single guild, it should be Temakh.<br /> <br /> Page 124 - In the Kefershaitan Stats insteading of Utterances it's written Nomenclature. And all the members of the Astral Lodge meret don't have their Temakh Virtues stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 11-06-2014, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:47:14-08:00","id":304686,"title":"","content":"Page 89: &quot;If more than one Deceived is present, the mummies gain Black Dice in order of highest Ren rating[.]&quot;Every Deceived has Ren 5 by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-08-2014, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:21:43-08:00","id":304697,"title":"","content":"Neph - Can't get quotes to work right now, but that's proper usage (and Shakespearean) of shall. You don't need &quot;who&quot; when it's expressing futurity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:30:41-08:00","id":304725,"title":"","content":"The Astral Lodge mummies are missing &quot;Blessed Is the God-King&quot; among their Utterances, despite all Deceived having that for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:34:46-08:00","id":304727,"title":"","content":"The Astral Lodge mummies also are missing their Guild Status Merit rating, while their cultists lack the &quot;Deceived Cultist&quot; Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T10:56:27-08:00","id":304733,"title":"","content":"Page 127 -- &quot;If 30 or more successes are gathered, the supplicant can forgo all of the above benefits and instead allow the stars to revel a lost secret.&quot; Should be &quot;reveal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:52:14-08:00","id":305032,"title":"","content":"Page 150 - &quot;The next time they purchase a new Affinity and allow Fate to dictate which one, they will instead gain a new Bane Affinity (tailored to their current <b>Morality</b>)&quot; It should be Memory<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:11:39-08:00","id":305047,"title":"","content":"Page 44 &quot;Great acts of obedience to their temakh grant a reset with no risk of Memory degeneration, while great sins prompt an immediate Descent Roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> I screwed this one up. The sentence should just read &quot;Great acts of obedience to their temakh grant a reset, while great sins prompt an immediate Descent Roll.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T15:19:28-08:00","id":305056,"title":"","content":"Page 77 -- &quot;In game terms, the difficulty to reveal information about members of this movement is increased by one to three depending on the piece of information with movement secrets having the greatest difficulty.&quot;<br /> <br /> Difficulty doesn't work this way. Perhaps: &quot;In game terms, actions taken to learn information about members of this movement suffer a -1 to -3 dice penalty, depending on the piece of information, with movement secrets assessing the greatest penalty.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:50:25-08:00","id":305104,"title":"","content":"Page 124: Kefershaitan's stat block contains the skill &quot;Leadership&quot;.<br /> Page 125: Kefershaitan has &quot;Nomenclature&quot; instead of &quot;Utterances&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:53:11-08:00","id":305106,"title":"","content":"While we're at it, Kefershaitan seems to have several Bane Affinities, something meant to be impossible (Ammut's Feast and Shadow Rending).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T16:57:30-08:00","id":305110,"title":"","content":"Kefershaitan's health is listed as 12, but he's Stamina 3. Given that he's Ka 4, it makes it seem like he was intended to have the Living Monolith Affinity, but it's not listed on his profile.<br /> <br /> Also, none of the Astral Lodge Deceived have an Immortal Virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T17:21:56-08:00","id":305122,"title":"","content":"Page 125: Obarous-Tet also has the &quot;Leadership&quot; skill.<br /> <br /> Then we have the following:<br /> <br /> Page 89: A Mummy of the Deceived may trade 1 Sekhem for 2 Black Die.<br /> Page 99 (Forgetting the Name, Tier 2): If the Deceived fails this roll she cannot target the same victim with this power for the remainder of the story, although she may immediately spend 1 Sekhem...<br /> Page 100 (Forgetting the Name, Tier 3): ...although she may immediately spend 1 Sekhem...<br /> <br /> These powers directly contradict page 34, Modified Advantage: Sekhem, where it states &quot;The Deceived use this trait like Arisen, but cannot voluntarily spend dots for any reason&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:22:38-08:00","id":305153,"title":"","content":"The short stories on pages 12, 16, 30, 84, 112, and 128 (and possibly 66, it's hard to tell) all seem to be missing the first line.<br /> <br /> And just to double-check, was it really intentional that the example Seba contain no sample 4 or 5 dot relics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:29:04-08:00","id":305197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/304560-book-of-the-deceived-errata-thread?p=305153#post305153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just to double-check, was it really intentional that the example Seba contain no sample 4 or 5 dot relics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space limitations. I'm working on a way to get them to you soon. I'm putting together a grab bag of assorted goodies you'll enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T19:39:17-08:00","id":305201,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, although I think a four and five dot one would have been more useful than doubling up on the lower dot Seba. Still, looking forward to the grab bag, whatever form it takes.<br /> <br /> Page 154: &quot;As she does so, a tremor shakes the chamber shakes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T22:17:18-08:00","id":305318,"title":"","content":"P. 63 &quot;Yellow and green make blue.&quot; should be &quot;Yellow and blue make green.&quot; Obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T05:04:08-08:00","id":305541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/304560-book-of-the-deceived-errata-thread?p=305122#post305122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we have the following:<br /> <br /> Page 89: A Mummy of the Deceived may trade 1 Sekhem for 2 Black Die.<br /> Page 99 (Forgetting the Name, Tier 2): If the Deceived fails this roll she cannot target the same victim with this power for the remainder of the story, although she may immediately spend 1 Sekhem...<br /> Page 100 (Forgetting the Name, Tier 3): ...although she may immediately spend 1 Sekhem...<br /> <br /> These powers directly contradict page 34, Modified Advantage: Sekhem, where it states &quot;The Deceived use this trait like Arisen, but cannot voluntarily spend dots for any reason&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noticed that, too. They aren't mine, but here's a suggested errata fix:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#262626\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;Once per scene, an Arisen may </span></span><span style=\"color:#262626\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">trade 1 Sekhem for 2 Black Dice as an instant action. Shuankhsen gain only 1 Black Die when they sacrifice Sekhem</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#262626\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">in this manner. Deceived can't do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> And for the other two: &quot;If the Deceived fails this roll she cannot target the same victim with this power for the remainder of the story, although she may reflexively spend two Ren points to force a re-roll of both dice pools with the Deceived at a -2 penalty.&quot;</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","user":"Nephilpal","date":". 11-07-2014, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T22:18:14-08:00","id":306415,"title":"","content":"Page 90: &quot;In addition to this <b>merits usually</b> effects,&quot; should be &quot;In addition to this <b>Merit's usual</b> effects,&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T00:05:27-08:00","id":306453,"title":"","content":"Less an Errata and more of a request: Between 45-65 Please list each Temakh by their common name as well, preferably as a subtitle. When I first went through this section I had to read several paragraphs to find out which ones were which. As they're referred to as &quot;painter' or 'philosopher' in the text before hand it's a little jarring to only have thier Iremite names visible as page headers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T08:24:34-08:00","id":306682,"title":"","content":"Page 37 - Memory 2 - Committing \u201csuicide\u201d by intentionally <b>burning out your Sekhem </b>or destroying your<br /> body.<br /> Deceived can't spend Sekhem dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:49:04-08:00","id":307914,"title":"","content":"Page 92 - Resplandecent Oracle -&gt;&quot;The mummy\u2019s body is saturated with prophetic power. Should a sapient being eat or <b>drink</b> any portion of it (such as a vampire drinking <b>his blood</b>), that being immediately becomes sick and spends the next turn unable to do anything besides forcefully vomit up the repast.&quot;<br /> <br /> I thought it was impossibly for a mummy to have his blood drunk, since their Sahu is basically a magical simulation of flesh, don't know if this is wrong or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T03:11:14-08:00","id":308014,"title":"","content":"Page 98-&gt; Call Down the Black Huriayh -&gt; I believe that the author of the Utterance when he mentions Duat might be mistaking it for Twilight.<br /> pg 109-&gt; 3rd paragraph &quot;balancing of <b>ma\u2019at\u2019s scales</b>&quot; it should be <b>Ma'at's.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 11-10-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:58:47-08:00","id":309731,"title":"","content":"Page 6, Left Column - &quot;The concert hall was a huge circle of <b>class</b> and steel, dark and closed to the public.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T03:37:18-08:00","id":310028,"title":"","content":"Page 63, left column - &quot;I had known this slit corpse would become the instrument of my betrayal, perhaps I would have turned away from this particular shade of red...&quot; feels like it should read &quot;Had I known&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 69, right column - &quot;<b>The</b> build shantytowns, ships of fools and anarchic cults...&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 69, right column - &quot;men and women brought up under new, <b>made</b> regimes&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 69, right column - &quot;Better to defile mystic vessels so that their enemy's dupes send a measure of poison with every one <b>the</b> sacrifice to the powers beyond.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 70, left column - &quot;He, who had been a slave the Keeper abused for pleasure had been bound to his lord through the Rite of Return. It was an insult from his betrayers.&quot; The main problem, I think, is the use of &quot;his&quot; to refer to Awa in the first sentence and, I think, the Keeper in the second. The first sentence is also worded rather clumsily.<br /> <br /> Page 70, right column - &quot;They made the lords of Irem to conquer humanity, break it with civilized ways, and send its dead to attend training <b>them</b> in A'aru.&quot; The word &quot;them&quot; should just be removed from this sentence.<br /> <br /> Page 70, right column - &quot;They were responsible for Awa's suffering, and the plight of all mortals, who've been thrown into the <b>service kings</b>, priests and presidents.&quot; Missing the word &quot;of&quot; in there.<br /> <br /> Page 72, left column, &quot;Impure Syllable&quot; description - &quot;If the corrupted vessel gets sacrificed to Duat, this counts as a use of the vessel, but inflicts a -3 dice penalty to the Descent check.&quot; Given the higher cost (a permanent dot of Willpower) for letting it go this far, and that feeding poison to the Judges seems a bit more impressive than merely tainting their servants, this should be a +3 bonus rather than a -3 penalty, surely? Descent checks get worse when more dice are rolled, rather than fewer.<br /> <br /> I'm also not entirely sure how this one is meant to work in general, because I was under the impression most vessels are sent to Duat when the Mummy returns to henet, implying that they have hit Sekhem 0 anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-12-2014, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T06:47:42-08:00","id":310203,"title":"","content":"page 130: &quot;He felt his rage growing has he thought about his former masters...&quot; should be &quot;He felt his rage growing <i>as</i> he thought about his former masters...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T20:47:10-08:00","id":310852,"title":"","content":"Page 72, right column - &quot;The Scions of the Emerald Ankh will generally opt for one of two extremes when establishing <b>a</b> influence over a territory...&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 74, left column - &quot;Therefore, <b>it likely</b> that members of this movement would have high levels of cult...&quot; should be &quot;it is likely&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 75 - &quot;Communion with one's temakh is conducted in private through private meditation...&quot; it's a little nitpicky, but one of those &quot;private&quot;s is redundant.<br /> <br /> Page 76, left column - &quot;By communing with his ancient memories, the undoing of the <b>Su Menent</b> could finally and <b>permanently undone</b> and the temakh know oneness again.&quot; Su-Menent should be hyphenated, and the word &quot;be&quot; is missing.<br /> <br /> Page 76, left column - &quot;...having all but abandoned their worship of <b>Nebshepsut's</b> original dissent.&quot; Should be &quot;Neshebsut&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:03:30-08:00","id":310926,"title":"","content":"Page 78, left column - &quot;Beyond this, the movement believes that civilization <b>is war's the</b> prize and battlefield.&quot; I think the words here need to be rearranged to &quot;is the war's prize and battlefield&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 79, left column - &quot;Legionnaires acquire Status, Allies and Contacts in these <b>group</b>.&quot; Should be &quot;groups&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T19:59:15-08:00","id":311873,"title":"","content":"Page 80, left column - &quot;Painted stele and dizzying reliefs engraved upon cyclopean monoliths are the signposts and masterworks offered to the temakh's need but <b>they are pointed the broken world called simply &quot;Before&quot;</b>...&quot; If I had to guess, I would say it's missing the word &quot;to&quot;, as in &quot;pointed to the broken world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 81, left column - &quot;In the past, those few who received such revelation and attempted to expose it, were taken by unlikely catastrophe, albeit one well and perfectly foreseen.&quot; The second comma breaks the sentence unnecessarily, it should read &quot;In the past, those few who received such revelation and attempted to expose it were taken by unlikely catastrophe, albeit one well and perfectly foreseen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 82, right column - &quot;(contained in <b>a odd</b> and winding epic poem known as <b>the &quot;The</b> Reverie of Meskhenet&quot;)...&quot; Two problems. It should be &quot;an odd and winding epic poem&quot;, and one of the two &quot;the&quot;s should be removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T00:32:31-08:00","id":312034,"title":"","content":"Page 88, left column - &quot;Yet the <b>difference showcase</b> the divergence of their purpose,&quot; either difference should be differences, or showcase should be showcases.<br /> <br /> Page 93, Whispers to my Body. Is the intent that the second dot point only refer to Deceived who have become Twice-Arisen? It states &quot;All rolls to recognize the Deceived by her physical appearance incur a -4 penalty unless she meticulously maintains her inherited appearance.&quot; This makes it sound like a blanket penalty, in that anytime anyone wants to try and recognise a Deceived with the Affinity they're at a -4 penalty, but the actual text description makes it sound like a far more marginal ability (when someone who knew the body the Deceived is wearing attempts to recognise them, that's when the -4 penalty kicks in). And I can't tell if this causes the changes wrought by the Temakh to undo themselves or not.<br /> <br /> Page 96, right column - &quot;Like all guilds, they have and employ their own Guild Utterance variant of Ancestry of Forgotten Stars (p. 121-122)...&quot; This sentence makes no sense. According to Guildhalls of the Deathless, the Su-Menent loathe telling other Guilds, even helping Maa-Kep Acolytes, that this Utterance <i>exists</i>. I certainly don't get where the &quot;Like all guilds&quot; part is coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}